WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.120
I want to take up in Volume 3, from February the 20th, 1900, and hear the subject is light.

2
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.760
My good Jesus continues to come, Louisa says, "After I received Communion, he renewed in

3
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:28.400
me the pains of the crucifixion, and I was left so numb that I felt the need for a relief,

4
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.000
but I didn't dare ask for it."

5
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.560
After what she'd been told, a few messages earlier, "After a little while Jesus came

6
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:46.040
back as an infant, as a baby, and he blessed me, milk flowed from his lips, and I drank

7
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.680
in large gulps, that most sweet milk that comes from his lips."

8
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.880
Now we need to remember that when Jesus comes as an infant, Louisa's going to be talking

9
00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:03.480
about either receiving milk from him or giving it, and you just need to remember that in

10
00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:09.960
the earliest stage of life that milk represents life itself.

11
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:17.480
So now while I was doing this, Jesus told me, "I am the flower of the celestial Eden,

12
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:25.960
and in the fragrance I spread is such that my perfume perfumes the whole of heaven and

13
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.480
keeps heaven captivated."

14
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:34.320
So the flower, I just want to give you one reference for that you could find from the

15
00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.440
Song of Songs, chapter 2 and verse 1.

16
00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:45.840
In the Song of Songs, he is the Rose of Charon and the Lily of the Valley.

17
00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:54.440
And since I am the lamp, that is the light of the world, that's John 812 and John 9.5,

18
00:01:54.440 --> 00:02:00.480
since I am the light that sends light to everyone, so much so as to keep them immersed in it,

19
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:05.920
all of my saints draw their little lights from me.

20
00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.680
So there's no light in heaven which has not been drawn from this lamp.

21
00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:17.440
This is described quite well in Revelation 21, verses 23 to 24, where in the New Jerusalem

22
00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:24.920
where everybody's living in the Divine will, there's no need for sunlight or daylight because

23
00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.000
Christ is our light.

24
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:34.920
And Louisa says, "I, yes, there's not even the smell of virtue without Jesus.

25
00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:39.720
And even if one went up to the highest heaven, there's no light without him, so he's the

26
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:48.280
Alpha and the Omega at the beginning and the end, that's Revelation 1, 17 to 18."

27
00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:55.080
Now we go on to February the 21st, 1900, and the subject is pure purity.

28
00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:59.320
And I want to give you a whole lot of references, and they're not all, indeed.

29
00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:07.360
Matthew 5, 8, only the pure and heart see God, Philippians 1, 10, and also chapter 4, verse

30
00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:10.560
8.

31
00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:18.840
The first letter of St. Paul to Timothy, chapter 1, verse 5 and chapter 5, verse 22, and the

32
00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:25.920
letter to Titus, chapter 1, verse 15, and Hebrews 10, 22, that's just to get you going

33
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.520
on this subject.

34
00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:34.560
This morning, my beloved Jesus began to make his usual delays.

35
00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.240
May he always be blessed, for he always starts from the beginning.

36
00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:46.120
Indeed, it takes patience, the patience of a saint to bear with him.

37
00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:51.520
I just find this absolutely unbelievable, and one would have to deal with Jesus to see

38
00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:54.080
how much patience it takes.

39
00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:59.000
One who was not experienced cannot believe it, and it's almost impossible not to have

40
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.480
a few hops with him.

41
00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:08.160
I think her language is absolutely fantastic, because it's revealing such a close relationship

42
00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:13.960
with Jesus, that it's telling all the rest of us that this relationship is real.

43
00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:19.200
This is not just mystical as in up in the air, and no contact with reality.

44
00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:26.760
This is very real, and they are both relating in a very real way to each other.

45
00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:32.200
And Louisa thinks she thought she had solved the privation problem, and then she finds

46
00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:38.600
that Jesus disappears again, and that's what she means by our back at the beginning, we're

47
00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:44.200
at the start again, and it's very difficult to have patience with him.

48
00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:49.840
That's because we're halfway through Volume 3, and she has not yet learned, he's told

49
00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:55.360
her in plain language, that she's to take it with patience, she's to surrender to the

50
00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:00.200
divine will, she's to offer it for love of him, and so on, and so on.

51
00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.160
That's okay if you're not going through the pain that she's going through and confined

52
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:09.600
to a bed with absolutely no distraction.

53
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:15.800
So the heading of the next paragraph is suffering for love of Jesus, it's the only acceptable

54
00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:17.800
motivation.

55
00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.320
Why?

56
00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:27.120
Because God is love, then Louisa said, "After being patient in waiting and waiting for

57
00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:32.960
him, finally he came, and he told me, 'My daughter, the gift of purity, in other words

58
00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:36.840
he doesn't deal with the privation, he's probably tired of it.

59
00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:42.960
My daughter, the gift of purity is not a natural gift.

60
00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:50.080
It's an attained grace, and it's obtained by rendering oneself worthy of sympathy, which

61
00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:57.280
I think is very interesting, I wouldn't have thought of this in two million years.

62
00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:05.640
The soul becomes worthy of sympathy through mortification and suffering, or how worthy

63
00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:12.040
of sympathy becomes the mortified and suffering soul, how striking she is, and I feel such

64
00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:18.440
sympathy as to go mad for her, and whatever she wants, I give her.

65
00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:25.400
When you are deprived of me, I want to add the words, 'Would you please suffer my privation

66
00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.920
for love of me?'

67
00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:33.560
Which is the most painful suffering for you, and I will feel more sympathy than before

68
00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:35.640
and grant you new gifts.

69
00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:40.320
So if only you would accept it, if only you would surrender to the fact that this is going

70
00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:47.940
to happen, and if only you would offer it for love of Jesus, then things can move on.

71
00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:52.720
Now she'll take one step forward and three steps backwards, just like we do on things

72
00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.400
we find difficult.

73
00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:03.840
So February the 23rd, 1900, the subject is discernment.

74
00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.600
This morning after I had almost lost the hope that blessed Jesus would come, all of a sudden

75
00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:13.320
he came and renewed in me the pains of the crucifixion.

76
00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:22.980
And he told me, 'The time has come, the end is approaching, but the hour is uncertain.'

77
00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.440
So I want to give you Amos 3-7 that the Lord never does anything without telling the prophets

78
00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:28.440
first.

79
00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:35.280
I also want to give you Revelation 11-1 when we're told the time has come.

80
00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.280
Okay.

81
00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:42.900
Now this is the beginning of the 20th century, and Jesus is saying it's the end times.

82
00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:48.440
Now lots of commentators around the world have caught on to the fact that we are in end time

83
00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:54.880
eschatology, and it's end time events that are happening around us, and the amount of

84
00:07:54.880 --> 00:08:00.040
chastisements that have happened on the earth is just off the richter scale, but we still

85
00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:05.040
don't get the message that if we repented things would change.

86
00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:09.080
So having been told that the time has come, the end is approaching, and that the hour

87
00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:14.320
is uncertain, Louisa said, 'Without paying attention to the meaning of the words that

88
00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:22.720
he spoke, I still had a doubt about whether I should apply them to the complete crucifixion

89
00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:26.920
that she's just experienced, or to the chastisements.'

90
00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:32.760
So she said to Jesus, 'Lord, how I fear that my state may not be the will of God, and she's

91
00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:37.240
doing at this for three volumes, and get used to it, and get patient about it, it's going

92
00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.360
to go on.'

93
00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:43.480
She does continuous discernment about this.

94
00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:45.440
She's right.

95
00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:50.960
The road she was on was different to everybody else, and while there were priests there, they

96
00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:58.440
could listen and offer their responses, but they couldn't tell her where she was going.

97
00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:06.080
Jesus said, 'The surest sign to know whether the state you are in is in the divine will

98
00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:11.000
is that you find the strength to sustain it.'

99
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:17.000
So you have the strength to do something, you may be suffering, it may cost you an awful

100
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:23.120
lot, but if you have the strength and the stamina to do it, and the certainty and the

101
00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:30.200
depths of your being that that's what you're called to, then it is the divine will.

102
00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:35.160
And Jesus said, 'When a person becomes intimate with the family, one no longer uses those

103
00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:40.000
formalities, those regards which they used before, even when they were a stranger.'

104
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.480
That's the way I do it.

105
00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:46.720
But nevertheless, this is not a sign that it's not the will of the family to have the

106
00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:51.120
person with them, or that they no longer love them as before.

107
00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:54.600
It's just the circumstances have changed.

108
00:09:54.600 --> 00:10:00.480
'Therefore,' he said, 'be at peace, let me do,' and he's going to plead with her so

109
00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:03.560
often to let him have his way.

110
00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:07.400
Do not want to rack your brains or trouble the peace of your heart.

111
00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:12.120
Now, the thing that was going to bring that, one of the things that was going to bring

112
00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:15.560
the 20th century down was rationalism.

113
00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:20.280
We want to rationalize everything, we want to bring all reality down within the confines

114
00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.800
of our tiny little brains.

115
00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:28.800
And if they don't fit within the confines of our little brains, we don't accept it.

116
00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:36.000
Therefore, truth and mystery and God and creation and life and everything is beyond us, because

117
00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:40.160
it's all part of this extraordinary mystery.

118
00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:47.200
So it begs your not to rationalize, and not to trouble the peace of our heart.

119
00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:53.760
If I want to give you SAM 131 there, my soul is like a weaned child on its mother's lap.

120
00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:58.160
At the appropriate time, you will understand how I'm working.

121
00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:06.800
It's not really until you get to the higher volumes that Louisa becomes not only fully

122
00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:13.280
aware of what he's doing, but realizes the plan that he's doing, and she becomes a completely

123
00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.840
different person at that stage.

124
00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:22.000
But what he does between now and then is that he explains everything little by little to

125
00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:27.240
her, and he's explaining it little by little to us, so I'm not going to jump ahead and

126
00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:34.320
tell you something ahead of Valian 3, I wouldn't be right, because we can only take things piece

127
00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:40.120
by piece according to the grace that's been given to us.

128
00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:47.240
So February the 24th, 1900, the subject is obedience, and the Lord has demanded that

129
00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:56.520
Louisa be the obedient one like himself, but this time she's having a problem.

130
00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.660
This morning I was all fear.

131
00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:05.040
Now we have to know that fear is the greatest weapon of the enemy, and if fear gets into

132
00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:10.760
us, he can produce all kinds of problems.

133
00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:13.520
I believe that everything was fantasy, she said.

134
00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:16.280
That is, the devil wanting to deceive me.

135
00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:20.720
So whatever I would see, I would despise, and I would be displeased.

136
00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:26.200
I saw the Confess replacing the intention that Jesus would renew in me the pains of the crucifixion,

137
00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.560
and I tried to resist.

138
00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:37.720
At first, blessed Jesus tolerated me, but since the Confessor kept repeating, they request.

139
00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:44.520
Jesus told me, "My daughter, at this time we are really going to fail in obedience.

140
00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:51.040
Don't you know that obedience must seal your soul, and that obedience must render the soul

141
00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:58.200
like soft wax in such a way that the Confessor may give to it the shape he wants."

142
00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:04.880
Now, even though she's at this very high level of union with God, and she has been gifted

143
00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:10.600
and graced to such an extraordinary degree, that doesn't mean that your will isn't completely

144
00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:15.400
free and that your emotions aren't free to express themselves, okay?

145
00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:20.560
And so the Lord is saying to her, "I need a deeper surrender.

146
00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:29.440
A surrender like melted wax has that you can put it into any shape at all."

147
00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:38.120
So you'll find as we go on in the volumes that Louisa is tested at the absolute extreme

148
00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.640
of obedience.

149
00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:45.520
It's one thing to call it heroism, but she's actually brought to the extreme where a human

150
00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:50.080
being can't go.

151
00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:58.840
So heedless of my resistance, Louisa says, "Jesus shared with me the pains of the crucifixion."

152
00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:07.480
And what you have there is that both God and Satan recognize the authority that a priest

153
00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:14.520
has in exorcisms, Satan will obey a command of a priest, and he won't obey a layman in

154
00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:15.520
