00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:59.880
You will have me in your own hands, and you can keep me there.

199
00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:03.880
So this is a wonderful thing that he is telling her.

200
00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:08.960
Now he says, "What is it that forms the beatitude of paradise?

201
00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:11.560
What is it that makes heaven happy?"

202
00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:15.080
He said, "Certainly it is my divinity."

203
00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:20.920
Now what would form the beatitude of my dear ones on the earth?

204
00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:25.680
With certainty, he said, "My will."

205
00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:28.280
My will can never escape you.

206
00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:35.080
Now as we go on in the volumes, he will explain that the divine will is in everything.

207
00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:41.600
It is in every tree, every shrub, every animal, every stone, every planet, every molecule

208
00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:43.480
of the air, water, etc.

209
00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:48.680
It is in every molecule of us, otherwise we would not exist.

210
00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:53.680
And if he took his will away from us, we would just simply cease to exist.

211
00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:59.000
So he said, "You'll always have the divine will in your possession."

212
00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:04.300
And if you remain within the circle of my divine will, now that circle we're going to

213
00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:13.520
hear more and more about as we go on, because it's the infinite dimension of God.

214
00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:18.840
And if you remain within the circle of my will, there you will experience joys most

215
00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:22.000
ineffable and pleasures most pure.

216
00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:31.920
Now that's expressed in Psalm 36 and it's 9 to 10 or 9 to 12, something like that, that

217
00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:37.480
we drink from the torrents of his delight.

